-- FIXTURES shared by the tests modules: named cases only, no directives, so this module
-- reports no assertions of its own. Read msig-cgl-tests-cover.l4's header for what the
-- baseline claim is and why a scenario is written as findings in front of it.

§ `Fixtures`

GIVEN parts       IS A LIST OF `A coverage part`
      designation IS A `A designation of the named insured`
      retro       IS A MAYBE DATE
      limits      IS A `The limits stated in the schedule`
GIVETH A `The policy as declared`
`a 2026 policy with` parts `, the named insured designated as` designation `, Retroactive Date` retro `, limits` limits MEANS
    `The policy as declared` WITH
        `coverage parts identified in the declarations`          IS parts
        `the named insured is designated in the declarations as` IS designation
        `the policy period begins`                               IS YMD 2026 1 1
        `the policy period ends`                                 IS YMD 2026 12 31
        `the retroactive date stated in the policy schedule`     IS retro
        `the limits stated in the schedule`                      IS limits

`both parts` MEANS LIST `the Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part`, `the Products and Completed Operations Liability Insurance Coverage Part`

`an organization` MEANS `an organization other than an individual, partnership or joint venture`

`a combined limit of 5 and 10 billion` MEANS `a combined single limit` 5_000_000_000 10_000_000_000

`the policy` MEANS
    `a 2026 policy with` `both parts` `, the named insured designated as` `an organization` `, Retroactive Date` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) `, limits` `a combined limit of 5 and 10 billion`

`a CGL-only policy` MEANS
    `a 2026 policy with` (LIST `the Comprehensive General Liability Insurance Coverage Part`) `, the named insured designated as` `an organization` `, Retroactive Date` NOTHING `, limits` `a combined limit of 5 and 10 billion`

`a policy issued to an individual` MEANS
    `a 2026 policy with` `both parts` `, the named insured designated as` `an individual` `, Retroactive Date` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) `, limits` `a combined limit of 5 and 10 billion`

`a policy issued to a partnership` MEANS
    `a 2026 policy with` `both parts` `, the named insured designated as` `a partnership or joint venture` `, Retroactive Date` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) `, limits` `a combined limit of 5 and 10 billion`

`a policy with Retroactive Date 1 June 2026` MEANS
    `a 2026 policy with` `both parts` `, the named insured designated as` `an organization` `, Retroactive Date` (JUST (YMD 2026 6 1)) `, limits` `a combined limit of 5 and 10 billion`

`a policy whose schedule states no Retroactive Date` MEANS
    `a 2026 policy with` `both parts` `, the named insured designated as` `an organization` `, Retroactive Date` NOTHING `, limits` `a combined limit of 5 and 10 billion`

`the ordinary facts` MEANS
    LIST `the insured is legally obligated to pay the sums claimed as damages`,
         `the harm results from an accident, including continuous or repeated exposure to conditions`,
         `the harm occurs within a nation or area described in the Policy`,
         `immediate notice of the harm has been given in accordance with the Conditions`

`the ordinary findings` MEANS
    append (map `it is the case that` `the ordinary facts`) (map `it is not the case that` `the facts the record may find`)

GIVEN person   IS A `A person claimed against`
      harm     IS A `A kind of harm`
      injured  IS A DATE
      claimed  IS A MAYBE DATE
      findings IS A LIST OF `A finding`
GIVETH A `A claim against an insured`
`a claim against` person `for` harm `on` injured `, claimed on` claimed `, where` findings MEANS
    `A claim against an insured` WITH
        `the person claimed against`                                      IS person
        `the harm`                                                        IS harm
        `the date the injury occurs`                                      IS injured
        `the date of the occurrence`                                      IS injured
        `the occurrence`                                                  IS "the occurrence"
        `the general conditions of exposure`                              IS NOTHING
        `the date the claim was first made in writing against an insured` IS claimed
        `the date an insured first became aware of circumstances which may give rise to the claim` IS NOTHING
        `the date written notice of those circumstances was given to the Company` IS NOTHING
        `the claim series`                                                IS NOTHING
        `the findings`                                                    IS append findings `the ordinary findings`

`bodily injury` MEANS `bodily injury, sickness or disease sustained by a person`
`physical damage` MEANS `physical injury to or destruction of tangible property`
`loss of use` MEANS `loss of use of tangible property which has not been physically injured or destroyed`

GIVEN findings IS A LIST OF `A finding`
GIVETH A `A claim against an insured`
`a bodily injury claim where` findings MEANS
    `a claim against` `the named insured` `for` `bodily injury` `on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, claimed on` (JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)) `, where` findings

GIVEN findings IS A LIST OF `A finding`
GIVETH A `A claim against an insured`
`a property damage claim where` findings MEANS
    `a claim against` `the named insured` `for` `physical damage` `on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, claimed on` (JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)) `, where` findings

GIVEN findings IS A LIST OF `A finding`
GIVETH A `A claim against an insured`
`a loss of use claim where` findings MEANS
    `a claim against` `the named insured` `for` `loss of use` `on` (YMD 2026 6 1) `, claimed on` (JUST (YMD 2026 7 1)) `, where` findings

-- The products hazard: harm arising out of the named insured's products, away from its
-- premises, after possession was relinquished (src:159-162).
`the products facts` MEANS
    LIST `it is the case that` `the harm arises out of the named insured's products, or reliance upon a representation or warranty made at any time about them`,
         `it is the case that` `the harm occurs away from premises owned by or rented to the named insured`,
         `it is the case that` `physical possession of those products had been relinquished to others when the harm occurred`

-- The completed operations hazard: harm arising out of operations, away from premises,
-- after all the operations under the contract were completed (src:74-80).
`the completed operations facts` MEANS
    LIST `it is the case that` `the harm arises out of operations, including materials, parts or equipment furnished with them, or reliance upon a representation or warranty made at any time about them`,
         `it is the case that` `the harm occurs away from premises owned by or rented to the named insured`,
         `it is the case that` `all operations to be performed by or on behalf of the named insured under the contract had been completed when the harm occurred`

GIVEN findings IS A LIST OF `A finding`
GIVETH A `A claim against an insured`
`a products claim where` findings MEANS
    `a bodily injury claim where` (append findings `the products facts`)

GIVEN findings IS A LIST OF `A finding`
GIVETH A `A claim against an insured`
`a products property damage claim where` findings MEANS
    `a property damage claim where` (append findings `the products facts`)

GIVEN findings IS A LIST OF `A finding`
GIVETH A `A claim against an insured`
`a completed operations claim where` findings MEANS
    `a bodily injury claim where` (append findings `the completed operations facts`)

GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A `The answer on cover`
`CGL:` claim MEANS `the answer under the CGL Coverage Part` `the policy` claim

GIVEN claim IS A `A claim against an insured`
GIVETH A `The answer on cover`
`P&CO:` claim MEANS `the answer under the P&CO Coverage Part` `the policy` claim

GIVEN f IS A `A fact`
GIVETH A LIST OF `A finding`
`only` f MEANS LIST `it is the case that` f

`the ordinary CGL claim` MEANS `a bodily injury claim where` EMPTY
`the ordinary products claim` MEANS `a products claim where` EMPTY


§§ `Fixtures for the amounts`

-- Rates of exchange are HYPOTHETICAL figures chosen to make the arithmetic visible:
-- 26,000 dong per US dollar, 19,000 dong per Singapore dollar. So US$250 is 6,500,000
-- and US$25 is 650,000; S$250 is 4,750,000 and S$25 is 475,000. The document gives no
-- rate (fork F5).
`the hypothetical rates` MEANS
    `Rates of exchange into dong` WITH
        `dong per United States dollar` IS 26_000
        `dong per Singapore dollar`     IS 19_000

GIVEN `bodily injury damages`   IS A NUMBER
      `property damage damages` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The sums for one occurrence`
`the ordinary sums, with damages of` `bodily injury damages` `for bodily injury and` `property damage damages` `for property damage` MEANS
    `The sums for one occurrence` WITH
        `damages because of bodily injury`                                   IS `bodily injury damages`
        `damages because of property damage`                                 IS `property damage damages`
        `fines, penalties, punitive, exemplary, treble or multiplied damages` IS 200_000_000
        `expenses incurred by the Company`                                   IS 50_000_000
        `costs taxed against the insured in a suit defended by the Company`  IS 10_000_000
        `interest accruing after entry of judgement and before the Company pays, tenders or deposits its part` IS 5_000_000
        `premiums on appeal bonds`                                           IS 2_000_000
        `premiums on bonds to release attachments, for an amount not in excess of the applicable limit` IS 1_000_000
        `the cost of each bail bond`                                         IS LIST 6_000_000, 3_000_000
        `expenses incurred by the insured for first aid to others at the time of the accident` IS 4_000_000
        `reasonable expenses incurred by the insured at the Company's request, other than loss of earnings` IS 8_000_000
        `the actual loss of earnings for each day`                           IS LIST 500_000, 400_000, 700_000
        `sums the insured voluntarily paid, assumed or incurred, other than for first aid` IS 30_000_000
        `expenses of withdrawal, inspection, repair or replacement, or of other preventive measures` IS 90_000_000

`the ordinary sums` MEANS `the ordinary sums, with damages of` 1_000_000_000 `for bodily injury and` 0 `for property damage`

GIVEN `bodily injury damages`   IS A NUMBER
      `property damage damages` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `The sums for one occurrence`
`damages alone of` `bodily injury damages` `for bodily injury and` `property damage damages` `for property damage` MEANS
    `The sums for one occurrence` WITH
        `damages because of bodily injury`                                   IS `bodily injury damages`
        `damages because of property damage`                                 IS `property damage damages`
        `fines, penalties, punitive, exemplary, treble or multiplied damages` IS 0
        `expenses incurred by the Company`                                   IS 0
        `costs taxed against the insured in a suit defended by the Company`  IS 0
        `interest accruing after entry of judgement and before the Company pays, tenders or deposits its part` IS 0
        `premiums on appeal bonds`                                           IS 0
        `premiums on bonds to release attachments, for an amount not in excess of the applicable limit` IS 0
        `the cost of each bail bond`                                         IS EMPTY
        `expenses incurred by the insured for first aid to others at the time of the accident` IS 0
        `reasonable expenses incurred by the insured at the Company's request, other than loss of earnings` IS 0
        `the actual loss of earnings for each day`                           IS EMPTY
        `sums the insured voluntarily paid, assumed or incurred, other than for first aid` IS 0
        `expenses of withdrawal, inspection, repair or replacement, or of other preventive measures` IS 0

GIVEN `combined`        IS A NUMBER
      `bodily injury`   IS A NUMBER
      `property damage` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A `Amounts already paid under the aggregate limits`
`already paid: combined` `combined` `, bodily injury` `bodily injury` `, property damage` `property damage` MEANS
    `Amounts already paid under the aggregate limits` WITH
        `under the combined aggregate`                     IS `combined`
        `under the bodily injury aggregate`                IS `bodily injury`
        `under the property damage aggregate that applies` IS `property damage`

`nothing paid yet` MEANS `already paid: combined` 0 `, bodily injury` 0 `, property damage` 0

-- Separate limits: bodily injury 2 billion each occurrence, 4 billion aggregate; property
-- damage 1 billion each occurrence, 2 billion aggregate.
`a policy with separate limits` MEANS
    `a 2026 policy with` `both parts` `, the named insured designated as` `an organization` `, Retroactive Date` (JUST (YMD 2020 1 1)) `, limits`
        (`separate limits for bodily injury and property damage` 2_000_000_000 4_000_000_000 1_000_000_000 2_000_000_000)
